<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    DEBUG BUILDS ONLY.

    This file lives in the `debug` source set (app/src/debug/res/xml/), so the
    Android build system merges it into debug APKs and NOWHERE ELSE. Profile and
    release builds do not contain this resource and do not reference it, so they
    fall back to the platform default: on API 28+ cleartext HTTP is blocked.

    Why it is needed: during development the QRIVO API runs as a plain
    `php -S` server over HTTP (see docs/RUNBOOK.md) at one of
      - http://10.0.2.2:8000    Android emulator's route to the host
      - http://<LAN-IP>:8000    physical device on the same network
    Without this, Android silently refuses those requests.

    Why it is a blanket permit rather than a host list: the LAN address changes
    per developer and per network, so an enumerated list would have to be edited
    by hand on every machine. The blanket permit is acceptable *precisely
    because* its scope is the debug build type. Do not move this file up into
    src/main/ — that would ship it in release.

    To tighten it for a specific machine, replace <base-config> with:
        <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
            <domain includeSubdomains="false">10.0.2.2</domain>
            <domain includeSubdomains="false">192.168.1.20</domain>
        </domain-config>

    Release builds must talk to the API over HTTPS, i.e. built with the
    API_BASE_URL dart-define pointing at an https:// origin.

    (Note for editors: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment, so this
    file spells command line flags without their leading dashes.)
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
